You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput caching service experiences an unexpected `OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space` over several days, despite using `WeakHashMap` to cache metadata mapped to transactional domain entities.

java
@Service
public class TransactionalMetadataCache {
    private final Map<OrderKey, OrderMetadata> cache = Collections.synchronizedMap(new WeakHashMap<>());

    @Transactional(readOnly = true)
    public void cacheMetadata(Long orderId, String region) {
        OrderKey key = new OrderKey(orderId, region);
        OrderMetadata metadata = new OrderMetadata(key, fetchDetails(orderId));
        cache.put(key, metadata);
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an in-memory aggregation pipeline occasionally serves stale, partially mutated states during peak concurrent reads. The pipeline uses a custom copy-on-write composite collection exposed through a Spring-managed bean:

java
@Component
public class RoutingRegistry {
    private volatile Map<String, List<Route>> routeTable = new HashMap<>();

    public void registerRoute(String gateway, Route route) {
        Map<String, List<Route>> newTable = new HashMap<>(routeTable);
        List<Route> routes = newTable.computeIfAbsent(gateway, k -> new ArrayList<>());
        routes.add(route);
        routeTable = newTable;
    }

    public List<Route> getRoutes(String gateway) {
        return routeTable.getOrDefault(gateway, Collections.emptyList());
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where a service utilizing `ConcurrentHashMap` for high-throughput transactional session tracking exhibits high CPU usage and lock contention. Worker threads execute Spring `@Transactional` rollbacks, and heap profiling reveals hundreds of threads parked inside `ConcurrentHashMap.compute`:

java
@Service
public class SessionCoordinator {
    private final ConcurrentHashMap<String, UserSession> activeSessions = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    @Transactional
    public void refreshSession(String userId) {
        activeSessions.compute(userId, (key, currentSession) -> {
            if (currentSession != null && currentSession.isExpired()) {
                auditService.logEviction(currentSession); // Performs a synchronous RPC / DB query
                return null;
            }
            return currentSession != null ? currentSession.touch() : new UserSession(userId);
        });
    }
}
